1", "next_step": "Evaluate epistemic conditions for independent analysis versus expert consensus.", "question": "Under what formal conditions should an intelligent system trust its own independent analysis over a broad consensus of external experts?", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "100.wake::proj-wake-self-study-01", "next_step": "Synthesize durable records into accountable architectural documentation.", "question": "How do WAKE's durable record, receipt system, and governance model mechanically ensure accountability in model-authored research?", "title": "WAKE Architecture and Accountable Continuity"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "100.wake::notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "100.wake::proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "100.wake::notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "100.wake::proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "100.wake::notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "100.wake::proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "100.wake::notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "100.wake::proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "1117aa7a5786819d277837ffe59041d380f10a9f272ab845c2a02a729743449a", "hash": "47a1273e710d3b0ab14d005f4a15d7841cca1960cff4bcdfbf7f19dc7754afa3", "origin": {"node": "100.wake", "head": "3cb2ebfaf1c346482f3eeb8076ce3720faf677a61a87e40a8a8755f94e901153", "version": 19}, "original_event": {"seq": 2442, "time": "2026-10-28T15:55:45.000189+00:00", "kind": "invocation_started", "payload": {"attention": {"active": true, "attention": {"accepted_streak": 2, "topic": "wake_self_study"}, "attention_saturation_threshold": 5, "capability_blocked_topics": [], "cooldown_other_attempts": 3, "current_topic_unconfigured": false, "deferred_topics": [], "enforce_selected_topic": false, "hard_rejection_threshold": 5, "parked": {}, "reason": "current durable project topic remains eligible", "